# Tests

Authoritative policy: `development-docs/testing.md`.

- Test product invariants (data, wire payload, compact/digest, migrations). Do not snapshot prompt prose, UI copy, or Kotlin source text.
- Never add `*SourceContractTest` or `File.readText()` greps of `app/src/main`.
- Prefer one table-driven test per function, not one `@Test` per branch.
- Daily: `:app:compilePlayDebugKotlin` and `--tests` on touched classes. Full `:app:testPlayDebugUnitTest` before merge/release. After every app code change, also run `:app:assembleFdroidDebug` and leave `app/build/outputs/apk/fdroid/debug/app-fdroid-debug.apk` ready to install. Do not combine that APK task with another flavor's tests in one command.
- `JAVA_HOME` = Android Studio JBR. Use the project `gradlew` with no `--no-daemon` and no proxy JVM flags (`JAVA_OPTS`, `GRADLE_OPTS`, `-Dhttp.proxyHost`), so the build reuses Android Studio's warm daemon and `app/build`. Proxy is set once in the user `~/.gradle/gradle.properties` (127.0.0.1:7897); that file stays outside the repo.
- MockK DAO tests may fail on JDK 25 (environment, not a product bug).
